; Test 30: the compiler's progress bar (#980).  stripe.bas: 80 lines, an
; include (TEDRUN:work/inc1.bb2, 12 lines) and a syntax error in its last
; line: CREATE EXECUTABLE, the error requester (OKAY) is dumped while the
; bar is still in the title area (closing the requester redraws it).  The
; original compiler (R5, C5) XORs the bar into TED's bitmap; blitz2-c
; reports its cells to TED-C (Cc), which draws the same picture; the
; original TED has no progress call, so Rc shows no bar.
; @source E stripe
; @file inc1.bb2 "b=b+1\x00b=b+1\x00b=b+1\x00b=b+1\x00b=b+1\x00b=b+1\x00b=b+1\x00b=b+1\x00b=b+1\x00b=b+1\x00b=b+1\x00b=b+1\x00"
; @xtra norunerr
; @est 8
; @expect absent stripe
; @fixed #980 R5-Rc Rc-Cc
timeout 10
wait req "OKEE DOKEE"
gad 1
wait screen
menu 4 2
wait freq "Name of Executable to create"
timeout 30
freq ok "stripe" "TEDRUN:work"  ; @ignore compilewindow
wait req "OKAY"
timeout 10
dump error
gad 1
wait screen
menu 0 9
wait exit
